1
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:42,820
It'll work out somehow.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,860
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,220
Look, even the burning steel will work out somehow,
eventually.

5
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:27,480
You understand, right? Got it, got it.
Once you do, follow me quietly.

6
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,840
Blow away this scorching heat!

7
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:58,900
It's so hot I'm going to die.

8
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,280
This heat really does take its toll,
doesn't it.

9
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:04,600
Shall we take a little break?

10
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:08,000
Here you go, that's 210 yen for two.

11
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:10,320
Wait here a moment.

12
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:13,020
Where's the money?

13
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,240
Oh, here it is, found it.

14
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,940
Here you go, Baidō.

15
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:22,640
S-senpai...

16
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:24,220
What's wrong?

17
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:32,000
Damn it! The ice cream I bought!

18
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,700
That's probably one of the causes, too.

19
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,000
Mirror buildings

20
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:41,200
They've suddenly increased lately,
haven't they?

21
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:44,180
reflecting the sunlight

22
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:46,820
lighting up even places
that should be in shade,

23
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,480
so the temperature just won't come down.

24
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:54,120
and because of that,
my room's a disaster too.

25
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,840
It's like a sauna in here.

26
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:06,440
Even with the curtains closed,
it's unbearably hot.

27
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,920
This is the cause.

28
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,920
That mirror building right in front of us...

29
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:21,340
Thanks to it,
it's like we're being lit by dozens of suns.

30
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,160
This is serious.

31
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:27,120
I don't need conditions.
This is basically harassment.

32
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:34,420
S-senpai? My head's starting to spin.

33
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,000
No! Is it heatstroke?

34
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:43,220
As expected, going into the
room during the day is dangerous.

35
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,280
Don't you have an air
conditioner or anything?

36
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:50,540
Nothing like that. This place is cheap, and
that's the only thing it has going for it.

37
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:53,420
Nobody living here has the
money to buy an air conditioner.

38
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:57,000
Hey, Hojo, are you off duty today?

39
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,640
Yes, I'm going to the library.

40
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:06,500
Let's go back to the police box too.

41
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:07,500
Yeah, let's.

42
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:10,360
What's wrong?

43
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:14,200
Hojo wasn't sweating at all, was he?

44
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,460
Now that you mention it...

45
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:21,860
With the mirror building's glare reflecting in,
it's gotten incredibly hot in here.

46
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,840
There's no way he shouldn't be sweating.

47
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:27,000
That bastard, could he possibly...

48
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,280
I'm coming in, Miss.

49
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:41,680
No way.

50
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:47,380
It's cool. It's like heaven!

51
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:51,000
The sweat is drying up right away.

52
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,620
Just as I thought.

53
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:57,060
Miss! You must be hiding an air conditioner!

54
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:58,900
W-what's your evidence?

55
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:00,720
This coolness is the evidence!

56
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,960
B-because we're running the electric fan.

57
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:07,860
Running a fan alone couldn't
possibly make it this cool!

58
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:12,820
Or does that fan have a
cooling function built in?

59
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,220
W-well, that's...

60
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,860
And that nabeyaki udon!

61
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:20,860
Only people with air conditioning
eat nabeyaki udon in the summer!

62
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,400
Search thoroughly!

63
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:32,420
There it is, the air conditioner!

64
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,380
The outdoor unit is
disguised as a mikan crate.

65
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,940
Everyone is suffering in this hellish heat,

66
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:45,720
and you're the only one
sitting here looking cool?

67
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:48,900
It was sent to me from home,
I swear it's true!

68
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:55,480
Then why is it secretly
installed where no one can see it?

69
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:58,660
If people find out it's an air conditioner,

70
00:05:58,660 --> 00:06:03,140
everyone will crowd into the room
and my peaceful life will be violated.

71
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,740
That's why you hid it, isn't it?

72
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:05,500
Gulp!

73
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:08,000
Have you no shame?
Are you even a police officer?

74
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:13,860
A police officer must always
consider the public good.

75
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:18,260
But right now,
you're putting your own interests first.

76
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,580
Someone like you has no right
to call himself a police officer.

77
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,120
So then,

78
00:06:30,620 --> 00:06:33,860
we'll be taking over this room.

79
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:43,600
Shall we go another round?

80
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:45,680
No, of course...

81
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:48,900
Even after moving my body this much,
not a single drop of sweat comes out.

82
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,980
All hail the air conditioner.

83
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:53,740
Air conditioning really is comfortable,
isn't it?

84
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:59,960
You shouldn't hog a life like
this all to yourself, Hojo.

85
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,160
Wow, it's cool!

86
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:10,260
So the rumor was true. Hojo really
has an air conditioner in his room.

87
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,440
Excuse me...

88
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:17,500
You should share some of
that coolness with us too.

89
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,300
It's here, it's here!

90
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,440
So this is the air-conditioned room

91
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,680
Hey, wait a minute, you guys!

92
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,060
You're all going to cram in there?
Hojo's going to say, "Wait!"

93
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:32,800
Hey, you're in the way!

94
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,300
I can't breathe!

95
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,880
Like this, I can't even play games.

96
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:46,240
But with this many people, it's pointless.

97
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,900
But the air conditioner
is only in this room.

98
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:57,700
Mind if we take all of
this ventilation duct?

99
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:59,020
Sure, go ahead.

100
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,940
What are you doing, old man?

101
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:08,500
We're sending the AC's
cool air to the other rooms.

102
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:15,320
Alright, switch it on!

103
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,180
The cool breeze...

104
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:24,060
We did it!

105
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:26,960
Yahoo! It worked, senpai!

106
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,140
I see.

107
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:30,700
Um... well, that is...

108
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:36,760
If that's blocked off, I don't think
any cold air will reach this room at all.

109
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:42,660
Chief, this cool air must be shared
fairly among everyone at the station.

110
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:43,820
Y-yes, I see.

111
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:48,340
But you've already monopolized
several days' worth of cool air.

112
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:51,360
So for now, you get none.

113
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,120
How long is "for now"?

114
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:57,140
It's about half a year, roughly.

115
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:58,640
Isn't it winter?

116
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:00,360
You brought it on yourself, idiot.

117
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:02,980
I'll hold onto this remote for now.

118
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:05,060
Don't go messing with the
switches without permission.

119
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,720
Senpai, are you really sure about this?

120
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,201
It's fine, it's fine.

121
00:09:10,251 --> 00:09:13,120
It's good for him to suffer a little heat.

122
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:15,100
Haaah...

123
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,540
It's hot...

124
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:24,480
It's cool. Paradise, pure paradise.

125
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:40,180
That bastard turned off the AC

126
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:43,460
Hey, Hojo, what's the big idea?

127
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,320
W-well, you see...

128
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,340
it suddenly stopped on its own.

129
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:50,800
Hey, what's going on?

130
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,580
What's wrong, senpai?

131
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:52,820
It's hot!

132
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:54,900
Hey, pull yourself together!

133
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,840
You're our only hope!

134
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,140
Yay!

135
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,020
Ooh!

136
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,240
The AC...

137
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:13,600
It was reckless to expect one air
conditioner to cover the whole room.

138
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:15,160
Whaaaat!

139
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:26,300
Damn, even in the shade it's not cool at all.
We really need an air conditioner.

140
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,160
What was that just now?

141
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:36,200
Mass production!

142
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:43,900
Hey, what are these air conditioners? They're taking
in the old ones from customers who bought new ones.

143
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:49,780
It's a waste, really. Most of them still work,
though. Is that true?

144
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:54,860
Alright, I'll take this air conditioner.
All of them? All of them?

145
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:59,840
Ryotsu, is it true you got a
large number of air conditioners?

146
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,500
Yes.

147
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:08,840
Please install one in my room too.

148
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,540
Me too, me too!

149
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,920
Of course, I'll install them for you.

150
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:16,740
But the installation fee
is 10,000 yen per unit.

151
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,700
Naturally.
I'm not interested in doing volunteer work.

152
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:25,160
If you don't like it,
you'll just have to put up with the heat.

153
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:28,320
Can't be helped, I suppose.

154
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:29,640
We'll pay.

155
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:32,640
Good, glad you understand.

156
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,000
Don't come back to life!

157
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:48,060
Now we can play games without a care.

158
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:52,460
Thank goodness.

159
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,120
Yes!

160
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,020
Plaro!

161
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,060
Exterior unit!

162
00:11:58,380 --> 00:12:01,460
Wow, having an air conditioner
really makes a difference.

163
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:03,820
Plus we got that extra income.

164
00:12:03,820 --> 00:12:04,380
Hehe.

165
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:08,200
Looks like we'll have a
comfortable dorm life from today.

166
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,580
It's still running.

167
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:12,920
What's wrong?

168
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,740
Auntie, what happened?

169
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,900
Did the breaker trip?

170
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:19,540
Looks like it.

171
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:21,220
Damn it.

172
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:22,340
Ugh.

173
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:24,600
Damn you.

174
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,660
The breaker's gone and blown, hasn't it?

175
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:47,420
Is it because we all
switched on the AC at once?

176
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:51,540
Old-model air conditioners really eat up electricity,
don't they?

177
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:55,020
I'll call the electrician, but...

178
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:57,960
They might be able to
tell what's wrong, though.

179
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,220
Eeeeeeeeh!

180
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,800
At this rate,
turning on the AC is no use to anybody!

181
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,160
Give us our money back!

182
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:09,680
Okay, okay, so come closer, then.

183
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:16,020
Iiii...

184
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:23,980
After all that hard work,
we're back to square one?

185
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:25,020
Damn it!

186
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:30,380
Ow

187
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:33,300
I only put water in a little while ago,
and it's already hot water.

188
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:35,560
It's more powerful than a gas stove.

189
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:39,400
If only we could put that
energy to some other use.

190
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,100
Exactly.

191
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:45,160
Put the energy to some other use...

192
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:48,000
So that's the way to do it.

193
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:54,660
This is payback for all the
torment you've put us through.

194
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:59,180
From now on,
I'm going to make full use of you.

195
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:20,240
This company is researching solar
panels for solar power generation.

196
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:22,000
How about it?

197
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:24,340
This is the Nikoniko Dormitory
in Katsushika Ward, right?

198
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:31,840
Wow, here we can get
more than enough sunlight.

199
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:35,180
Indeed,
it's the perfect place to test solar panels.

200
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:37,720
Right? Leave it to me.

201
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:41,200
I'll thoroughly test your
company's new product for you.

202
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:52,080
Start generating power.

203
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,560
The needle jumped all at once!

204
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:58,500
That's an incredible
amount of power generated!

205
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:01,200
Alright,
turn on the air conditioners in every room.

206
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:01,780
Yes.

207
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:08,960
Alright, next.

208
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:25,200
Don't worry. There's still
plenty of room to go full power.

209
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:26,778
I see.

210
00:15:26,828 --> 00:15:30,500
With this,
we've said goodbye to the sweltering summer.

211
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:38,849
This dorm really is comfortable.

212
00:15:38,899 --> 00:15:41,100
It's cooler than my apartment.

213
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:44,960
Right? It should be the
coolest place around here.

214
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:47,060
Even when you exercise,
you don't break a sweat.

215
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:52,720
We generate enough power that
it's fine to set the AC to maximum.

216
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,960
Why don't you move in too?

217
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,120
I'll think about it.

218
00:16:03,060 --> 00:16:05,500
It's still incredibly hot outside,
as always.

219
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:10,740
Poor guy, having to head home
through this damn sweltering heat.

220
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,260
Damn.

221
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,820
I prepared something just in case
something like this would happen.

222
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:27,680
It's a cooling suit made from
leftover air conditioners.

223
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:34,180
Cold air comes out of the cooler on your back,
travels through the hose, and flows into the suit to cool your body.

224
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:36,440
But it looks awfully stuffy, doesn't it.

225
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:38,700
That machine on your back looks heavy.

226
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,920
It really is heavy.

227
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,000
It's an old-model cooler,
so it can't be helped.

228
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:48,480
Just standing here makes you sweat.

229
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:51,400
Just wait, I'll make it happen today.

230
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:55,200
In an instant, sweat...

231
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:58,980
No matter how much I move now,
I'll never break a sweat.

232
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:00,820
That doesn't look good for your body.

233
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:04,660
I didn't pack in batteries,
since it would get too heavy.

234
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:06,900
The cord is plenty long.

235
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:09,580
Go take a little walk around here.

236
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:18,440
Even with the sun this strong,
it's not hot at all!

237
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:21,680
No, it's actually too cold.

238
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,460
We have to raise the temperature.

239
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:29,380
Damn, I can't reach it, it's cold!

240
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,100
They're rushing back!

241
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:39,320
I'm freezing to death!
Hurry up and turn it off!

242
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:42,080
Listen, was there a problem
with the switch's position?

243
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:45,940
This time it should be fine, right?

244
00:17:47,620 --> 00:17:48,920
Mm, perfect!

245
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,960
Well, I'm going to take
a little walk around.

246
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,760
What are you doing, Ryo-san?

247
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,580
Just a little experiment.

248
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:07,040
This is pretty good.

249
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:09,100
It's like the heat outside is a lie.

250
00:18:09,860 --> 00:18:11,900
It's getting a little hot.

251
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:13,260
Let's make it today.

252
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:17,020
With this, the sweat dries up in an instant

253
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:18,360
dries up

254
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,420
It's not working.

255
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:22,400
What's going on?

256
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:26,020
He's back.

257
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,700
He looks dazed.

258
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:30,760
I wonder what happened.

259
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,820
It's so hot I'm going to die.

260
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:37,680
What?

261
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:40,860
The cord...

262
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:46,500
Come on, Auntie, you can't do that!

263
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,660
You went and pulled
the cord out on your own.

264
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:50,960
Is that so?

265
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:53,580
Hold on, I'll collect it right now.

266
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,920
Are you okay, Volvo?

267
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:12,780
It's hell, I can see the Grim Reaper.

268
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:16,640
Dragging a power cord
around is way too dangerous.

269
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:19,260
Wouldn't it be better to have
a built-in battery after all?

270
00:19:19,260 --> 00:19:22,300
Our dormitory has more
electricity than we could ever sell.

271
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:24,220
It would be a waste not to use it.

272
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:27,700
Then why don't you actually sell it?

273
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:28,940
What did you say?

274
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:32,440
I think the electricity
generated by solar power

275
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:35,140
should be bought by the power company,
you know.

276
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:36,340
Really?

277
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:38,340
Yes!

278
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:40,680
It's from the electric company.

279
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:43,800
There's 200,000 yen!

280
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:46,040
It really adds up, doesn't it?

281
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:49,500
No good,
this little amount is no good at all.

282
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:51,580
We need to raise the power output even more.

283
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:53,960
Raise the power output, you say?

284
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:58,060
Because we made full use of the sunlight
reflecting off that Mirror Building.

285
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,060
That's how we got this much power output.

286
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:01,680
We can't go any further than this.

287
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:05,460
That's right, there's a limit
to how much sunlight we can use.

288
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:09,600
Then we'll just gather the light.

289
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:21,620
Go ahead and start it.

290
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:23,660
It's that one.

291
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:28,840
Maybe this angle?

292
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:29,200
Hey.

293
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:36,320
Here it comes! Yes, we did it!
The power output is going up.

294
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:42,220
Hey, are you in the factory?
Stop lazily reading books and help out.

295
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:48,440
What? We need to gather the light.
Make everyone who's left help out.

296
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,780
It's hot.

297
00:20:58,440 --> 00:21:00,100
Why do I have to do it too?

298
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:04,680
Okay, okay.

299
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:06,820
Good, good.

300
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,920
No good, no one's answering.

301
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:19,080
If we don't contact them soon,
it's going to be a disaster.

302
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:22,000
Today at 1:45 PM.

303
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:25,700
In other words, five minutes from now, the light
reflected off the surrounding mirror buildings

304
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:27,240
will concentrate on the Nikoniko Dormitory,

305
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:30,260
and it'll instantly get incredibly hot.

306
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:33,320
Nobody's picking up at
the dorm phone either.

307
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,040
We have no choice but to fly there directly.

308
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:38,240
Get a helicopter ready right away.

309
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:38,940
Yes!

310
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:46,300
This'll boost the power output even more!

311
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:54,480
What is that?

312
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:01,080
This much should be enough.

313
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,260
It's really hot

314
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:06,740
Should we head back to the room?

315
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:12,060
This is gathering the light.

316
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:14,520
If we keep this up,
something terrible will happen.

317
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,460
Please stop, senpai.

318
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:20,640
There's a massive updraft right here.

319
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:23,280
What is that guy doing?

320
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,240
The temperature keeps climbing!

321
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:28,060
We've got less than a minute left!

322
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:29,260
Is this going to be okay?

323
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,740
Stop! Please stop it right now!

324
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:44,400
Boss! It's impossible! There's no time!

325
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:06,280
This is incredible!
We're getting an enormous amount of power!

326
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:17,820
Senpai!

327
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:20,940
I can't take it anymore, I'm pulling out!

328
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:31,200
Too much light is gathering...

329
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,120
The Nikoniko Dormitory...

330
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:53,860
It's melting.

331
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:23,780
Uh, let's see uh, well...

332
00:24:23,780 --> 00:24:25,260
Excuse me, may I order?

333
00:24:25,260 --> 00:24:26,120
Welcome!

334
00:24:26,120 --> 00:24:28,440
Then ato-maki, salmon roll, salad roll.

335
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:30,280
Anything rolls...
what should I get, I wonder?

336
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:31,680
Right!

337
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:34,240
Do you have California rolls?

338
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:36,300
We don't have California rolls.

339
00:24:37,260 --> 00:24:39,000
This isn't America, you know!

340
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,400
I'm sorry.

341
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:44,360
Uh, excuse me...

342
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,280
Welcome!

343
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:49,840
Then, kushiage, kakiage, katsuage.

344
00:24:50,940 --> 00:24:53,660
What was it again? What do you recommend?

345
00:24:54,780 --> 00:24:56,960
Just be careful with the fried bones.

346
00:24:56,960 --> 00:25:00,680
Was that a dad joke?

347
00:25:00,680 --> 00:25:02,400
Yeah, that one's...

348
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:04,780
I have no idea what's going on.

349
00:25:04,780 --> 00:25:08,380
What's this? What's this?

350
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:09,160
Seriously?

351
00:25:09,420 --> 00:25:13,220
Come on in, come on in, go ahead!

352
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:18,000
Welcome, welcome, come on in, please!

353
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,500
Come in, come in, welcome!

354
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:22,600
Welcome, come on in!

355
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:25,300
Come in, come in, welcome!

356
00:25:25,820 --> 00:25:27,200
Welcome!

357
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:31,540
Summer vacation is almost over, too.

358
00:25:31,540 --> 00:25:34,400
Why does Lemon get to be taken everywhere?

359
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:37,300
Citrus is taking us on a trip?

360
00:25:37,740 --> 00:25:39,780
And we get to meet a real ninja?

361
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:43,280
Yay! Lemon has admired
ninjas for a long time!

362
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:46,360
Next time: Lemon becomes Funō Ichi Ninja!

363
00:25:46,760 --> 00:25:47,320
See you then.

364
00:25:53,980 --> 00:25:59,200
Thank you for watching.

